ded joint withstands the same pressures as the pipe itself.</p><h2>Hydraulics, Hygiene, and Environmental Sustainability</h2><p>Drinking water safety and energy efficiency are top priorities at K-Aqua. The mirror-smooth inner surface of our PP-R and PPRCT pipes features an extremely low roughness of only k = 0.007 mm. This effectively prevents limescale encrustation and stops the formation of breeding grounds for biofilms and Legionella.</p><p>Furthermore, polypropylene is physiologically completely safe, taste- and odor-neutral, and free of heavy metals and plasticizers. K-Aqua piping systems are certified worldwide according to the strictest testing standards (including DVGW, KIWA, WRAS). The system is also ecologically convincing: the polymer is 100% recyclable and has an excellent eco-balance in the manufacturing process compared to metal pipes.</p><h2>Important Installation and Planning Guidelines</h2><p>To ensure proper function over the guaranteed 50-year service life, the following points must be observed during installation:</p><ul><li><span class=\"font-semibold\">Pressure Testing:</span> After assembly, the piping network must undergo pressure testing in accordance with DIN 1988 / DIN EN 806.</li><li><span class=\"font-semibold\">Thermal Insulation:</span> Hot water and heating pipes must be properly insulated according to applicable energy efficiency regulations (e.g. GEG) to minimize heat loss.</li><li><span class=\"font-semibold\">UV Protection:</span> For outdoor open installations, UV-protected pipes must be used or appropriate covers provided.</li></ul>",
